The export has 427 rows and 412 unique report IDs merged into #4471. It shows two distinct cause groups, not one parser bug. The table deduplicates overlapping rows by report ID and assigns causes from tenant locale, booking form, and report channel—not `meta.intakeTag`.

## Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first

For tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, the shared parser can flip day and month. This group covers 379 reports across 11 tenants: 204 app, 150 email, and 25 form reports. Track it separately from booking-v3 form reports.

[Issue #1 — shared parser (379 reports)](https://github.com/pawelrychlicki/megadev/issues/1).

## booking-v3 gives day-first tenants a month-first hint

The booking-v3 form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the affected tenants use day-first locales. This separate group covers 33 form reports: `alder.physio` (12), `copper.studio` (11), and `pale.harbour` (10).

[Issue #2 — booking-v3 hint (33 reports)](https://github.com/pawelrychlicki/megadev/issues/2).

